        <section class="c-page__body" id="maincontent">
            <section class="c-container c-container--has-bg-color u-pure-white-bg c-container--inset "
    id="details">

    
    <section class="c-container__blocks">

        <div class="o-layout o-layout--center">
                            <div class="o-layout__item u-2/3@desktop">
    <div class="c-col c-col-text-area u-transparent-bg" >
    	
        
                    <p class="c-drop-cap lead-p">Experience a ‘burst of late summer sun’ ★★★★ (<i>Time Out</i>) in the Globe Theatre with Shakespeare’s love-struck comedy <b>As You Like It</b>,<b> </b>that&#8217;s<b> </b>packed with ‘fizzing chemistry’ ★★★★ (<i>WhatsOnStage</i>).</p>
<p>Watch as an eighteenth-century court transforms into a forest of freedom, painted live on stage every performance, and join us for &#8216;an entertaining frolic in the woods&#8217; ★★★★★ (<em>London Theatre Reviews</em>).</p>
<p>Rosalind is suffocating in the newly reigning Duke’s court. Surrounded by high wigs and even higher tempers, when egos come to a head, Rosalind and Celia flee into the Forest of Arden. They arrive, stumbling into a world where opposites attract, revelry is king and love is easy to find, if hard to recognise…</p>
<p>Co-directed by ‘powerhouse team’ ★★★★★ (<em>The Reviews Hub</em>) <strong>Sean Holmes</strong> (<em>Romeo and Juliet, Pinocchio</em>, Globe) and <strong>Charlie Josephine</strong> (<em>Pinocchio</em>, Globe, <em>Cowbois</em>, RSC/Royal Court), discover this bold take on Shakespeare’s famous comedy.</p>
<blockquote><p><strong>“We that are true lovers run into strange capers.”</strong></p>
<p>Act II, scene 4</p></blockquote>
            </div>
</div>
                            <div class="o-layout__item u-1/3@desktop">
    <div class="c-col c-col-text-area c-col--has-bg-color u-dark-raspberry-red-bg" >
    	
        
                    <p class="lead-p"><strong><i class="fal fa-info-circle"></i> DETAILS</strong></p>
<p><i class="fal fa-ticket"></i><strong> TICKETS</strong><br />
<strong> Galleries (Seating) </strong>£89– £29*<br />
*includes a £3 per order transaction fee and a £1 per ticket restoration levy</p>
<p><strong> Standing </strong>£10, £5 (Get two free standing tickets for one performance a year with <span role="presentation"><a id="OWAb863c6cf-715c-908c-577d-a91318287b54" class="OWAAutoLink" title="https://www.shakespearesglobe.com/join-and-support/membership/" href="https://www.shakespearesglobe.com/join-and-support/membership/" data-auth="NotApplicable"><u>Membership</u></a></span>)</p>
<p><i class="fal fa-map-marked"></i> This event is <strong>on-site</strong> in the  <a href="https://www.shakespearesglobe.com/venue/globe-theatre/">Globe Theatre</a></p>
<p><i class="fal fa-clock"></i> <strong>Running time </strong>2 hours 40 minutes, including a 20 minute interval</p>
<p class="smaller-p"><strong><a href="https://www.shakespearesglobe.com/policies/terms-conditions/">Terms and conditions</a></strong><br />
<span data-teams="true">All under 16s must be accompanied by an adult, and cannot be sat separately.</span></p>
<p>Photography: Felicity McCabe<br />
Art Direction: Doug Kerr</p>
<p class="lead-p">Part of <a href="https://www.shakespearesglobe.com/discover/blogs-and-features/2026/01/26/imagine-together-2026/"><strong>Summer 2026</strong></a></p>
            </div>
</div>
